# Pillar Voice

### School Election Management System

Pillar Voice is a digital school election management system developed using Python and MySQL.
The system was designed to replace the traditional ballot-based election process with a more organized digital voting workflow.


## Features

* Student, teacher and administrator authentication
* Candidate management
* Digital vote casting
* MySQL database integration
* Automated vote counting
* Overall election results
* House-wise results
* Position-wise results
* Election data management


## Technologies Used

* Python
* MySQL


## How It Works

The system provides separate workflows for students, teachers and administrators.
Students can authenticate themselves and cast their votes digitally. Election data is stored in a MySQL database, while administrators can manage election records and generate different types of result tallies.


## Real-World Deployment

Pillar Voice was developed as a school project and was subsequently adopted by my school (NPS International, Mysore) for conducting elections.
The school transitioned from its traditional ballot-based voting process to digital voting using the system.


This project was developed as a CBSE Class XII Computer Science investigatory project during the 2025–26 academic year.
The project provided practical experience in Python programming, relational database design, Python–MySQL integration and developing a software solution for a real-world use case.
